Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Maria, your second example is a good illustration of why some truncation
is usually beneficial.  However, whether you truncate 5% or 10% in these
examples really shouldn't matter.  Either choice results in detection
functions that fit the data very well, and your estimates of density
should be virtually the same, whether you use 5% or 10%.

Steve Buckland

